## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses practical Azure OpenAI engineering skills for data generation with governance, privacy, and observability.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant data policy gating
- PII redaction using Text Analytics
- Grounding with Cognitive Search and versioned KB
- Auditable logging to Data Lake

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example pseudo-code: gate -> redact -> search -> openai
function handleInput(input, tenant) {
  if (!policyAllows(tenant, input)) throw new Error('Not allowed');
  const redacted = redactPII(input);
  const kb = searchKB(redacted, tenant);
  return callOpenAI(redacted, kb);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test PII redaction completeness?
- How would you manage KB versioning and cache invalidation?

Why This Is Asked

Assess the ability to design a compliant, multi-tenant AI service on Azure with strong data isolation, governance, and cost controls.


## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation across storage, prompts, and model deployments
- Data governance and lineage with Purview
- PII handling and privacy-by-design in prompts
- Cost controls and API Management gating


## Code Example

```javascript
// Tenant routing sketch
function routeForTenant(req) {
  const tenant = req.headers['X-Tenant'];
  if (!tenant) throw new Error('Missing tenant');
  return {
    deployment: `openai-${tenant}`,
    container: `cosmos-${tenant}`
  };
}
```


## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test for cross-tenant data leakage?
- How would you implement per-tenant budgets and fail-closed behavior?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes architectural decisions for multi-tenant Azure AI deployments with strict data residency, governance, and explainability requirements. It tests ability to plan region-aware routing, tenant-scoped knowledge bases, identity boundaries, and end-to-end auditing.

## Key Concepts

- Data residency and customer-managed keys (CMK) for storage
- Region-local Cognitive Search indexes per tenant
- Region-aware model routing for Azure OpenAI
- Per-tenant RBAC using Azure AD
- Explainability logging to Data Lake with traceability
- End-to-end testing including latency, privacy, and auditability

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo region routing for tenants
function getTenantRegion(tenantId) {
  const regionMap = {
    't1': 'eastus',
    't2': 'northeurope'
  };
  return regionMap[tenantId] || 'eastus';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate cross-region consistency and prove data residency?
- What failure modes require circuit breakers and fallback paths, and how would you implement them?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical understanding of cloud AI wiring, cost controls, and data safety in a beginner-friendly Azure setup.

## Key Concepts
- Azure OpenAI Service behind API Management
- Blob Storage for knowledge base
- Azure Cognitive Search for grounding
- PII redaction in input
- Per-tenant token-budget gate

## Code Example
```javascript
// Redaction example
function redactPII(text) {
  return text.replace(/\b\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}\b/g, "[REDACTED_DATE]");
}
```
```javascript
// Budget guard example
function withinBudget(nextTokens, budget, spent) {
  return spent + nextTokens < budget;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end RAG pipelines with governance in a realistic Azure stack.

## Key Concepts
- Retrieval augmented generation, vector search, API Management, per-tenant residency, secret redaction, monitoring.
- Access controls, cost vs latency trade-offs, data provenance.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Redact secrets from user prompt
function redactPrompt(input){
  return input.replace(/(password|token|secret)\s*=\s*\S+/gi, '$1=REDACTED');
}
```

```javascript
// Simple guardrail stub: block disallowed topics in response
function guardResponse(text){
  const forbidden=[/internal-credential|secret-key/i];
  for(const f of forbidden){
    if(f.test(text)) return text.replace(f, 'REDACTED');
  }
  return text;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle index refresh cadence vs API latency in a large codebase?
- What metrics would you collect to detect degradation in retrieval quality?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design end-to-end Azure OpenAI-powered data-governance tooling that handles multi-tenant isolation, secure KB grounding, and robust testing.

## Key Concepts
- Data lineage ingestion and normalization across Synapse/Data Factory.
- Versioned KB in Azure Blob and Cognitive Search integration.
- Per-tenant isolation with Key Vault-backed Cosmos DB storage.
- Prompt engineering with fallback chains and confidence scoring.
- Data redaction and auditability.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for gap-filling using KB
async function fillLineageGap(partialLineage, kbClient) {
  if (partialLineage.isComplete()) return partialLineage;
  const kb = await kbClient.query(partialLineage.pattern);
  return partialLineage.enrich(kb);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure the accuracy of enrichment?
- How would you handle cycles or conflicting KB results?

